cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use timecourse-patterns, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "timecourse-patterns: temporal clustering of omics timecourses"
abstract: >-
  A Snakemake workflow that takes a counts matrix and a samplesheet from a
  timecourse experiment and returns dynamic features grouped into named
  trajectory classes, with publication figures and an HTML report. Assay
  agnostic: features may be genomic regions or genes. Supports multi-arm
  designs sharing a single unstimulated baseline.
type: software
authors:
